From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Braga?= <code@andrebraga.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:27:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf: qcom: add the LLCC per-CPU read-miss PMU

Recent Qualcomm LLCCs count the read misses of each CPU, in a 24-bit
counter per CPU with no overflow interrupt; Qualcomm's vendor kernels
expose it as llcc-pmu-ver2. Memory latency governors gate DDR votes on
these misses, and perf can profile a CPU's DRAM reads with them.

Add it as a perf PMU: an event counts the CPU it is opened on, and
counters are folded into 64-bit totals, so several events on one CPU
see every miss. While events exist a deferrable timer folds the
counters before they saturate; CPUs only miss while they run, so the
timer never needs to wake an idle system.
